<%#
  One collapsible role section of the project Files panel.

  Locals: key (a stable slug for the section), label, group (attachments), open (Boolean).

  EXTRACTED BECAUSE THERE ARE NOW TWO CALLERS — the ROLE_LABELS loop and the Backups section — and
  they must render identically apart from being open or closed. Inlining the second was the obvious
  thing and would have meant two copies of the tile markup, which is how the Detach button ends up
  on one of them and not the other.

  `open` is a real HTML attribute, so a closed section costs nothing at render time and the browser
  keeps the toggle state for the life of the page. It is NOT persisted across loads: that would need
  a cookie per section per project, and the panel's default (everything open but Backups) is the
  answer for almost every visit.
%>
<section class="attachment-group">
  <details <%= "open" if open %>>
    <summary class="attachment-group-head">
      <%= label %> <span class="muted">(<%= group.size %>)</span>
    </summary>
    <div class="attachments-grid">
      <% group.each do |att| %>
        <% node = @att_nodes[att.node_id] %>
        <% ext = File.extname(node.name).delete(".").upcase.first(4) %>
        <div class="attachment-tile">
          <%# data-download-url is what puts "Download" in the right-click menu (filemenu#open).
              Same blob endpoint the file page's own Download button uses, with ?download=1 so the
              disposition is `attachment` whatever the type would otherwise allow inline. %>
          <%= link_to file_path(att.node_id), class: "grid-card file-cell",
                      data: { thumbs_target: "cell", node_id: att.node_id, ext: ext,
                              action: "contextmenu->filemenu#open",
                              note_url: file_notes_path(att.node_id),
                              download_url: blob_file_path(att.node_id, download: 1) } do %>
            <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: @thumbs.thumb(att.node_id), ext_label: ext %>
            <span class="grid-name"><%= node.name %></span>
          <% end %>
          <div class="tile-meta">
            <%= button_to "Detach", attachment_path(att), method: :delete, class: "linkbtn danger",
                          form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Detach #{node.name}? (the file itself is kept)" } } %>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
